  "enhanced_information": "Urea is produced in the liver as a waste product of protein metabolism, then transported to the kidneys for excretion. It is not degraded to ammonium in the urea cycle. Urea is a polar molecule due to the presence of the amino group and is derived from ammonia and carbon dioxide in the liver. It contains one carbonyl group and one amino group, not two ketone groups. Evidence paths confirm its role in liver and kidney function."
